+# Educational points series and AI-drafted cards (7.0.75)
+
+Follows 7.0.74. Changed on request: the list is no longer fixed at five points,
+and each point is covered while the narration reaches it, across the whole video.
+
+## Who gets it
+
+Only **educational** videos: content type `education`, and a preset that is not a
+story preset. Presets containing `story`, `cartoon`, `kids`, `fairy` or `animation`
+are excluded (for example `cartoon_story` and `cinematic_story`). Story and
+cartoon videos keep their current cards. Educational videos with the default
+`cinematic_realism` preset do get the cards.
+
+## What appears on screen
+
+- **Points series.** 2–8 points, in spoken order. The panel opens when the first
+  point starts, highlights the point being covered (soft bar, accent colour), moves
+  to the next point when the narration moves on, and closes after the last point.
+  Each point is shown for the time it is spoken. The font shrinks as needed so up to
+  eight points fit; a list that cannot fit at a readable size fails with a clear message.
+- **Single-point cards** (`takeaway`, `tip`, `warning`), at most four, and only
+  before the first point or after the last point. Cards that would overlap the series
+  are dropped and counted in `speech_cards.json` as `dropped_overlapping_cards`.
+
+## Who writes the copy
+
+The card draft uses the **drafting model chosen in Create** (the "Drafting model"
+selector): Gemini Web (default), ChatGPT Web, ChatGPT/OpenAI API, Indus AI, Gemini
+API, Groq, Grok or Ollama. The choice is saved with the job as `card_draft_provider`.
+The prompt includes the video topic, so copy stays on the topic. Only facts stated in
+the narration are allowed.
+
+## Validation rules (checked before rendering)
+
+- 2–8 points; each point at most 60 characters; series title at most 60.
+- Points must not overlap and must be in spoken order.
+- Coverage: the first point starts within the first quarter of the narration, and the
+  last point ends after 70% of it.
+- Single cards: 1.5–6 seconds, at most 80 characters, takeaway/tip/warning only.
+
+## Animation
+
+- The series panel opens once (scale-in with fade), then stays while the highlight
+  moves, and closes once (shrink with fade).
+- Single cards pop open and closed.
+- The FFmpeg renderer supports `open`, `close` and `pop` modes. Middle segments of the
+  series carry no animation, so the highlight changes without the panel re-animating.
+
+## Not in this release
+
+- Language editions still use the 7.0.73 card path. Educational series are not
+  applied to edition copies yet.
+- The narration script itself is not rewritten by this change. Only the on-screen copy
+  is drafted by the chosen provider.
+- A real AI draft and a full render on the user's footage still need the user's test.
+
+## Install
+
+From 7.0.74: `python3 ../AutoVideoAI-v7.0.75/tools/update_v774_to_v775.py .` (dry run),
+then with `--apply`. Stop the dashboard first.
